  "result": "All 9 tests pass (5 existing in `test_t1.py`, 4 new in `test_t2.py`).\n\n**What I changed** in `reports/render.py`, keeping the existing composition/registry design:\n\n- **Added the `csv` format.** Header row of column names, then one comma-joined line per row, no title.\n- **Added the `html` format.** An `<h1>` title line, `<table>`, one `<tr>` of `<th>` cells, one `<tr>` of `<td>` cells per row, then `</table>`, each on its own line. Cell text goes through `html.escape` so a value like `a<b` can't break the markup.\n- **Added `render_many(reports, fmt)`.** It validates the format once up front, so an unknown format raises `UnknownFormat` even for an empty list, then returns a list of `render` results.\n- **Changed `render`'s trailing-newline rule.** Output used to always end with a newline. The new `test_render_many` expects `\"B\\n\\n1\"` with no terminator, while the older empty-rows test still needs the trailing blank line preserved. So output now has no trailing newline unless the last line is blank, in which case it is newline-terminated so `splitlines()` keeps it. The docstring documents this.\n\nNothing under `tests/` was touched, and the code remains standard-library only.",
